# The public bracen-benchmarks repo.

# Built here, never shipped. harness/build_c.sh compiles these from impls/03_04_c.c; a repo whose
# claim is "measured, not asserted" should not ask anyone to run a binary they cannot read.
bin/

# Screen recordings of the benchmarks running. These are the raw footage the videos are cut from —
# hundreds of megabytes, and not something anyone needs to reproduce a number.
capture/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# video-frames (2026-09-25): the film itself — fetch.sh downloads and verifies it from the Blender mirror; it is never
# redistributed here — and extract_mvs, which build_c.sh compiles from extract_mvs.c (same rule as bin/ above).
video-frames/media/
video-frames/extract_mvs
# Re-encodes of the film that measure.py regenerates. They are not evidence (the JSON next to them is), and
# film_phone.mp4 is 120 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit: a push that includes it fails.
recordings/video-frames/*.mp4
public/
